Cell["\<\
Definition: an infra-point is one vertex of the substrate, carried by its \
label verbatim.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"18d2e70d-260b-4876-af88-1b90fd44d317"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A point is a vertex. The head is a token of the scene language and holds no \
value of its own. A condition on a point, such as its distance to another \
point, is an assertion of the scene. A construction on a graph rarely has one \
answer, but the multiplicity does not live in this head: a family of \
candidate points is a vertex ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "438efdff-eefc-4187-813d-aa6a1e4da78b"],
 ", and a measure on vertices is a density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"<|", 
   RowBox[{"v", " ", "->", " ", "m"}], "|>"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1bb3997d-a721-4fb6-9661-46e53ff99868"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"74d22ee1-bc81-4370-94dd-bc0a8e214ef8"],

